        "original_id": "87f858a4-75be-5b5d-b112-57c3f3edbf62",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Scientific Games Corporation, Bally Technologies\n- Products: electronic gaming machines, table games, iGaming products, iLottery products, instant lottery games, lottery gaming systems, terminals, internet applications, server-based interactive gambling terminals, gambling control systems, scratchcards\n- Topics: scratchcard terminology\n\nFacts:\n- Scientific Games Corporation offers products including electronic gaming machines, table games, iGaming and iLottery products, instant lottery games, lottery gaming systems, terminals and services, internet applications, server-based interactive gambling terminals, and gambling control systems.\n- A scratchcard is a small card, usually made of thin paper-based card for competitions or plastic to conceal PINs, with one or more areas of concealed information that can be revealed by scratching off an opaque covering.\n- Scratchcards are also called scratch offs, scratch tickets, scratchers, scratchies, scratch-its, scratch games, scratch-and-win games, instant games, or instant lottery in different places.\n- Bally Technologies is owned by Scientific Games Corporation.",
